{{!-- v3 Features tab.

      FIFTH PART MIGRATED, and the densest float debt v3 has taken on so far: 374 lines, 14 floats,
      7 clearfixes and 7 inline styles on v2 — every single one of which is in the EXPERIENCE LEDGERS
      at the bottom (measured: `pullLeft`/`pullRight` at feature.hbs:300-362, `clearareaBox` at
      299-346, `style=` at 300-338, nothing above line 298). The item lists above them are already
      flex, inside `feature_item.hbs`, and are not touched.

      SHELL/ROW SPLIT (add-pc-sheet-v3 D5), AND THE TWO PLACES IT BENDS
      ----------------------------------------------------------------
      Nine item blocks and the Shadow area are `{{> …}}` includes of shared partials
      (`feature_item.hbs`, `feature_shadow.hbs`), passed exactly the arguments v2 passes, in the same
      order, including the `valuefirst` / `valuefallback` distinction whose whole point is that the
      two views of the same item cannot disagree. Those partials are untouched, so a fix to a Feature
      row still reaches both sheets from one file.

      It bends twice, in the two places v2 authors a row INLINE and there is nothing to share:

        1. THE CONNECTION ROSTER. `feature.hbs:235-262` builds the entry — portrait, body, description,
           external link — with no partial behind it, so a v3 shell either duplicates it or invents one.
           Duplicated, deliberately, with every class kept (`sheet-boxcontainer connection-entry`,
           `shape-panel-image connection-portrait`, `connection-body`, `connection-description`,
           `connection-link`): they are styled in `css/wod.css` under "START Connection roster" and that
           styling is flex, not float, so there is nothing here for v3 to improve by re-authoring it.
           `feature_item.hbs` is still the include inside the row.

        2. THE EXPERIENCE LEDGERS, which are the actual work. See below.

      NO `data-action` AND NO `data-*` IS ADDED OR LOST. `itemCreate` (with `data-origin="feature"`),
      `itemEdit`, `itemDelete` and the `data-itemid`/`data-type`/`data-area`/`data-sheet` set are
      exactly v2's, and `data-area` is carried even though NO JavaScript reads it (verified: the only
      `dataset.area` in the tree is in `module/handlebars.js`, on markup this tab does not produce).

      WHAT CHANGES, AND WHY EACH ONE
      ------------------------------
      1. THE UNCONDITIONAL "Feature" HEADER IS GONE. `feature.hbs:6-8` draws a `headlineRow` over
         nothing whenever the actor holds no Feature at all — and on this tab that is common, because
         the experience ledgers below are what a starting character actually has. The tab title in the
         header replaces it, which is the same string the nav already shows (`wod.tab.features`,
         pc-actor-sheet.js) and is now in the content area where the other four migrated tabs put it.

      2. ONE EMPTY STATE FOR THE ITEM LISTS (D9), and its wording is checkable rather than decorative.
         `CreateHelper.CreateButtonsNotev2` offers Background, Merit, Flaw and Other Traits to every
         splat, plus the two experience entries; Blood Bond, Boon, Oath and the wraith kinds are gated
         per line, so the string names only the universal four and the experience pair. The tab is
         NEVER hidden: `data-origin="feature"` is the only in-sheet route to authoring any of them.

         The gate is `and`+`not`, not `or`, for the reason combat.hbs records at line 29: Foundry's
         `or` folds over `arguments`, which includes the options object, so `(or a b)` is
         unconditionally true. `and` is unaffected, so the De Morgan form is the one that works.

         It covers the ITEM LISTS only. The Shadow area gates itself (`hasshadowarea`) and the ledgers
         always render, so a wraith with no Features still gets an honest "no features yet" above a
         Shadow area that has content — which is true of both.

      3. FOUR THINGS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT "FIXED", each because it is a decision someone already made:
         - Backgrounds, Merits, Flaws and Other Traits render here AND on the Stats tab, from one
           `prepareAdvantageLists` call. That is the tab reorganisation and it is sequenced separately.
         - The wraith Shadow area draws its two group headings even when both lists are empty, and
           `feature_shadow.hbs:14-16` says why. Untouched.
         - Bloodbound / Boon / Oath render on `length > 0` for EVERY splat. The create buttons were
           gated by splat; the render deliberately was not, because hiding an item that exists also
           hides the delete button that is the only way to remove it.
         - The ledgers' progressive disclosure already works. The MECHANISM is untouched — see below.

      THE EXPERIENCE LEDGERS: A DOM CONTRACT THAT IS NOT A CSS SELECTOR
      ----------------------------------------------------------------
      This is the part of the file to read before editing it. The unfold machinery is INHERITED
      JavaScript and it navigates by SHAPE, not by class:

          `ItemHelper._onTableCollapse`  : `et.parent().parent().parent().siblings('.' + dataset.type)`
          `_restoreUnfoldState`          : `ele.parentElement.parentElement.parentElement`, then that
                                           element's siblings filtered by `classList.contains(type)`
                                           — and ONLY for buttons whose `data-sheet` equals
                                           `CONFIG.worldofdarkness.sheettype.mortal`
                                           (pc-actor-sheet.js:545-581)

      So three things must hold, and none of them is checkable by `binder-selector-check.py`, which
      verifies that `.unfold.button` is PRODUCIBLE and cannot verify an ancestor count:

          a. the toggle sits EXACTLY three elements deep inside the header block;
          b. that header block and the ledger are SIBLINGS with a common parent;
          c. the ledger carries the literal class named by `data-type` (`addexp` / `spentexp`) plus
             `hide`, which is the collapsed default `_restoreUnfoldState`'s else-branch re-asserts.

      The class NAMES of the three wrappers are free — v2's happen to be `.pullLeft` / `.clearareaBox`
      / `.headlineRow`, i.e. the floats — so they are replaced with v3 names at the same depth and the
      floats go with them. The shape is preserved to the element.

      THE TOGGLE STAYS AN `<i>`, AND THAT IS A DEFECT LEFT IN PLACE ON PURPOSE. It cannot be reached
      by any keyboard — the same defect v3 fixed on the Effects and Gear rows by making the control a
      `<button>`. It is NOT fixed here, and the reason is specific rather than timid:
      `_onTableCollapse` swaps `fa-angles-right`/`fa-angles-down` on `event.currentTarget`, i.e. on
      the bound element itself, so the Font Awesome class cannot move to a child the way it does on
      every other v3 button. And a `<button>` carrying that class renders NOTHING legible:
      `css/wod.css:399` is `.wod20 button:not(.header-control) { font-family: var(--main-font) }`,
      specificity (0,2,1), which out-ranks `.fa-solid`'s (0,1,0) — so `::before`'s `"\f101"` is
      painted in a text font and comes out as a tofu box. Making it work needs `content: none` on the
      button's own pseudo-element PLUS a child chevron PLUS a state-class rotation: three interacting
      rules, with no automated gate that renders CSS, layered onto the one mechanism on this tab that
      already works. The honest trade is to leave it and say so. Reverting this decision is swapping
      `<i …>` for `<button type="button" …>` and writing those three rules — `type="button"` is not
      optional there, a bare `<button>` in an ApplicationV2 `<form>` defaults to `type="submit"`. --}}
<section class="tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-drop-area="true">

	<div class="v3-tabhead">
		<h2 class="v3-tabtitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.tab.features"}}</h2>

		{{!-- Same two v2 defects as every other tab's create control: a 3x-scaled glyph floating in
		      the corner, carrying `aria-hidden="true"` ON THE INTERACTIVE ELEMENT, which removes a
		      working control from the accessibility tree entirely. --}}
		<button type="button" class="v3-add" data-origin="feature" data-action="itemCreate">
			<i class="fa-solid fa-square-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span>{{localize "wod.labels.add.item"}}</span>
		</button>
	</div>

	<div class="v3-tabmain">

		<div class="v3-section">

			{{!-- A Background is DOT-RATED, so `valuefirst=item.system.value`: the rating is read
			      BEFORE `system.level`, the opposite order from merits and flaws below. The full
			      measured reasoning — all 96 compendium backgrounds ship `level: '0'`, the character
			      exporter hard-codes it, and the system's own create button writes `level: 1` as a
			      placeholder that never tracks the dots afterwards — is at `parts/feature.hbs:10-30`
			      and is not repeated here, because it belongs with the partial that consumes it. --}}
			{{#if (gt backgrounds.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each backgrounds as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked unnamedtitle="wod.notes.unnamedbackground" edittitle="wod.labels.edit.background" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.background" showtype=true valuefirst=item.system.value}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- Merits and flaws are POINT-COSTED, so `level` first and `valuefallback` second — the
			      same order `stats_feature_row.hbs` uses for these two lists on the Attributes tab, so
			      the two views of one item cannot print different numbers. --}}
			{{#if (gt merits.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each merits as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.merit" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.merit" showtype=true valuefallback=item.system.value}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if (gt flaws.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each flaws as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.flaw" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.flaw" showtype=true valuefallback=item.system.value}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- Blood Bond, Boon and Oath render for EVERY splat on `length > 0`, and that is
			      deliberate: the CREATE buttons are gated per line, the render is not, because hiding
			      an item that exists also hides the delete button that is the only way to remove it. --}}
			{{#if (gt bloodbounds.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each bloodbounds as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.bloodbound" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.bloodbound" showtype=true}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if (gt boons.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each boons as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.boon" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.boon" showtype=true}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if (gt oaths.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each oaths as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.oath" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.oath" showtype=true}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- Passions and Fetters — the wraith's own rated Feature kinds. Dark Passions are NOT
			      here: `add-wraith-shadow-budget §2.2` moved them into `feature_shadow.hbs` precisely
			      so they cannot sit in the next row of the same list as the Passions and be read as
			      one pool. Both pass `valuefirst`, like the Backgrounds block and for the same
			      reason. --}}
			{{#if (gt passions.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each passions as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.passion" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.passion" showtype=true valuefirst=item.system.value}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if (gt fetters.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each fetters as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.fetter" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.fetter" showtype=true valuefirst=item.system.value}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- The relationship roster: ONE sub-kind (`wod.types.connection`) grouped by
			      `system.relation`, with each group's name and dots taken from the actor's own
			      Background item. The reasoning is at `parts/feature.hbs:184-223`; what matters here
			      is that the ENTRY is authored inline in both files because no partial exists for it.

			      The portrait is NOT a picker and carries no `data-edit`, so it gets no `pointer`
			      class — clicking it does nothing, and the sheet must not offer a hand cursor that
			      says otherwise. The description is triple-stashed because it is already-enriched
			      HTML off the sheet context. --}}
			{{#if hasConnections}}
				{{#each connections as |group|}}
					<div class="headlineGroup splatFont">
						{{group.label}}
						{{#if group.rating}}{{#numLoop group.rating}}&#9679;{{/numLoop}}{{/if}}
						({{group.count}})
					</div>

					<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
						{{#each group.entries as |item id|}}
							<div class="sheet-boxcontainer connection-entry">

								<div class="shape-panel-image connection-portrait">
									<img class="profile-img shape-image{{#unless item.hasPortrait}} shape-image-empty{{/unless}}"
									     src="{{item.portraitSrc}}" title="{{item.name}}" alt="{{item.name}}" />
								</div>

								<div class="connection-body">

									{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs"
										actor=../../actor item=item locked=../../locked
										edittitle="wod.labels.edit.connection"
										deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.connection"
										showtype=false}}

									{{#if item.hasDescription}}
										<div class="connection-description">{{{item.enrichedDescription}}}</div>
									{{/if}}

									{{#if (ne item.system.link "")}}
										<a class="connection-link" href="{{item.system.link}}" target="_blank">{{localize 'wod.connections.link'}}</a>
									{{else}}
										<span class="information-area connection-link">{{localize 'wod.connections.nolink'}}</span>
									{{/if}}

								</div>

							</div>
						{{/each}}
					</div>
				{{/each}}
			{{/if}}

			{{#if (gt othertraits.length 0)}}
				<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
					{{#each othertraits as |item id|}}
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.othertraits" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.othertraits" showtype=true}}
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if (and (not backgrounds.length) (not merits.length) (not flaws.length) (not bloodbounds.length) (not boons.length) (not oaths.length) (not passions.length) (not fetters.length) (not othertraits.length) (not hasConnections))}}
				<p class="v3-empty">{{localize "wod.notes.empty"}}</p>
			{{/if}}

		</div>

		{{!-- The Shadow's own area — Archetype, Angst, Dark Passions and Thorns, with the Shadow's
		      10-point pool named and the Dark-Passion ceiling shown. It gates itself on
		      `hasshadowarea`, so it renders for a wraith (including empty, which is the normal state
		      of a freshly imported one) and for nobody else. Untouched. --}}
		{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_shadow.hbs"}}

		{{!-- ── THE EXPERIENCE LEDGERS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
		      Read the DOM-contract section in this file's header before changing the nesting below.
		      The toggle must stay exactly three elements deep inside `.v3-xphead`, `.v3-xphead` must
		      stay a SIBLING of the ledger, and the ledger must keep the literal `addexp`/`spentexp`
		      class its toggle's `data-type` names, plus `hide`.

		      v2 laid this out as `.clearareaBox > two .pullLeft[style="width:50%"]` with four more
		      floats and three inline margins inside each. A two-column grid replaces all of it, and
		      folds to one column when the sheet is narrow — which the two hard 50%s never did. --}}
		<div class="v3-section v3-xpgrid">

			<div class="v3-xpcol">
				<div class="v3-xphead">
					<div class="v3-xpheadrow">
						<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expearned"}}</h3>
						<span class="v3-xptotal">{{getTotalExperience actor "earned"}}</span>
						<div class="v3-xptoggle">
							<i class="icon unfold button pointer fa-solid fa-angles-right"
								title="{{localize 'wod.labels.show.experience'}}"
								data-sheet="{{config.sheettype.mortal}}" data-type="addexp"></i>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="hide addexp v3-xpledger" data-area="addexp">
					{{#if (getEarnedExperience actor)}}
						<table class="v3-table v3-xptable">
							<caption class="v3-sr-only">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expearned"}}</caption>
							<thead>
								<tr>
									<th scope="col">{{localize "wod.labels.description"}}</th>
									<th scope="col" class="v3-num">{{localize "wod.experience.experience"}}</th>
									<th scope="col" class="v3-actioncol"></th>
								</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
								{{#each (getEarnedExperience actor) as |item id|}}
									<tr>
										<td>
											{{#if (ne item.system.description "")}}
												{{item.system.description}}
											{{else}}
												{{localize "wod.notes.descriptionmissing"}}
											{{/if}}
										</td>
										<td class="v3-num">{{item.system.amount}}</td>
										<td class="v3-rowactions">
											{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
												<a class="item-edit" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.edit.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemEdit"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i></a>
												<a class="item-delete" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.remove.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemDelete"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-trash-can"></i></a>
											{{/if}}
										</td>
									</tr>
								{{/each}}
							</tbody>
						</table>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="v3-xpcol">
				<div class="v3-xphead">
					<div class="v3-xpheadrow">
						<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expspend"}}</h3>
						<span class="v3-xptotal">{{getTotalExperience actor "spent"}}</span>
						<div class="v3-xptoggle">
							<i class="icon unfold button pointer fa-solid fa-angles-right"
								title="{{localize 'wod.labels.show.spentexp'}}"
								data-sheet="{{config.sheettype.mortal}}" data-type="spentexp"></i>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="hide spentexp v3-xpledger" data-area="spentexp">
					{{#if (getSpendExperience actor)}}
						<table class="v3-table v3-xptable">
							<caption class="v3-sr-only">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expspend"}}</caption>
							<thead>
								<tr>
									<th scope="col">{{localize "wod.labels.description"}}</th>
									<th scope="col" class="v3-num">{{localize "wod.experience.experience"}}</th>
									<th scope="col" class="v3-actioncol"></th>
								</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
								{{#each (getSpendExperience actor) as |item id|}}
									<tr>
										<td>
											{{#if (ne item.system.description "")}}
												{{item.system.description}}
											{{else}}
												{{localize "wod.notes.descriptionmissing"}}
											{{/if}}
										</td>
										{{!-- An Experience row that is not yet marked spent prints the word
										      rather than a number, exactly as v2 does — so this cell is NOT
										      always numeric and the tabular-figure column is still correct
										      for the ones that are. --}}
										<td class="v3-num">
											{{#if item.system.isspent}}
												{{item.system.amount}}
											{{else}}
												{{localize "wod.notes.unspent"}}
											{{/if}}
										</td>
										<td class="v3-rowactions">
											{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
												<a class="item-edit" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.edit.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemEdit"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i></a>
												<a class="item-delete" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.remove.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemDelete"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-trash-can"></i></a>
											{{/if}}
										</td>
									</tr>
								{{/each}}
							</tbody>
						</table>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			</div>

		</div>

	</div>

</section>
